PHYSICAL SUMMARY

- Tidal radius decreases monotonically with orbital approach, consistent with
  strengthening external tidal field during MW–M31 infall.
- Stripping is episodic and strongly peaked at pericentre passages.
- Mass loss is inside-out: outer halo layers become unbound first.
- Tidal heating is impulsive and radially structured, strongest in outer halo.
- Tidal tensor anisotropy peaks during closest approach, indicating highly
  directional gravitational distortion.
- Unbound particles form coherent tidal streams in both configuration and
  phase space, consistent with classical merger dynamics.

