TECHNICAL NOTES

- Enclosed-mass potential approximation introduces smoothing assumptions.
- Tidal tensor computation is computationally expensive and noise-sensitive.
- COM-frame velocity subtraction may degrade during late-stage merger overlap.
- Time axis assumes uniform snapshot spacing; should be explicitly verified.

